A||N||4||Formula88||88 Wheel Alignment Verification?||||5||
Z||000000||Formula88||11-16-2001||11:39 AM||||Ok, I'm getting my Formula aligned tomorrow.  I did a search and come up with these numbers.  Can someone please verify that this is the correct and current alignment data?  I want to make sure the shop is using the right info.<P>FRONT<BR>Toe (per wheel): 0.3* +/- 0.2* total<BR>Camber: 0* +/- 0.5*<BR>Caster: Coupe w/ Manual Steering: +3.0* +/- 0.5*<BR>Caster, GT & Formula: +5.0* +/- 0.5*<P>REAR<BR>Camber: -1.0* +/- 0.5*<BR>Toe (per wheel): 0.15* +/- 0.1*<P>It's a bit confusing since it lists Manual Steering for the coupe.  Presumably the Formula and GT's were supposed to have power steering.  I take it I use the Formula/GT settings, even if they list power steering?<P>Please, if someone could verify this for me today.  My appt. is at 1P.M. on Sat., so I want to go in there with the data in hand and not sound like an idiot.<P>THANKS!||||reg||5
Z||000001||DRH||11-16-2001||12:08 PM||||That matches the factory service manual. Well, actually the manual has +/- 2*, not .2*, total toe on the front.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> That HAS to be a misprint.<P>Good question on the caster. I knew the GT/Formula were 5* instead of 3*, but never realized that might have been planned to be used WITH power steering. I wonder how they were adjusted from the factory??? The higher caster should be better from a performance stand point, but will make it a LITTLE harder to turn stopped/slow. I doubt it would be enough extra effort to worry about about... I would go with 5*.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Indiana_resto_guy||11-16-2001||03:46 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DRH:<BR><B><P>Good question on the caster. I knew the GT/Formula were 5* instead of 3*, but never realized that might have been planned to be used WITH power steering. I wonder how they were adjusted from the factory??? The higher caster should be better from a performance stand point, but will make it a LITTLE harder to turn stopped/slow. I doubt it would be enough extra effort to worry about about... I would go with 5*.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I think this accounts for the 15 inch tires on the GT & Formulas. Coupes have 14 inch, as you know.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||avengador1||11-16-2001||05:10 PM||||As for the power steering, no Fieros came from the factory with power steering.Except for maybe one or two very rare ones.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Formula88||11-16-2001||05:31 PM||||I know they didn't have power steering from the factory, but they were going to.  That's why I'm asking.  The specs list GT/Formula and Coupe with manual steering.  I suspect they were expecting the GT/Formula to have power steering.  So I was wondering if the different tires or the power steering could be the reason for the different specs.<P>Regardless, I'm going with the GT/Formula specs and see how that works.<BR>||||reg||1
